<task id="033" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Graph 5.101 → 6.5.0 + Kiota 1→2 (transitive); retire the 7 Kiota pins + NoWarn</title>
    <phase>P3 Test green + re-baseline</phase>
    <gate>030 complete (full suite green on net10 / Graph 5.x baseline)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Breaking SDK major on a core integration (Graph auth + SPE + mail + jobs); brownfield; bff-api; security-relevant (CVE closure mechanism changes).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The break is mechanical + closed-scope per the break-assessment; no architectural judgment beyond the enumerated call sites.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial: runs AFTER the net10 retarget is proven green (030) so net10 and the Graph major stay independently verifiable; 031/032 measure the post-033 package graph.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030</deps>
    <tags>dotnet, bff-api, packages, migration, security, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Migrate the BFF from `Microsoft.Graph 5.101.0` to `6.5.0` (re-pull the latest 6.x before pinning) — which pulls `Microsoft.Graph.Core 4.0.1` and transitive `Microsoft.Kiota.* 2.0.0` — then DELETE all 7 direct `Microsoft.Kiota.*` `PackageReference`s (now satisfied transitively at 2.0.0, which is > the 1.22.0 CVE floor) and confirm `NoWarn=NU1903` is gone (task 004 removed it; if present, remove). This is an owner-approved fold-in of a formerly-deferred optional major (design §6.4), justified by the break-assessment sizing it as MECHANICAL (`notes/graph6-kiota2-break-assessment.md`): the hard v4→v5 Kiota rewrite is already absorbed, direct Kiota usage is 100% on the stable side of the 2.0 break (zero hits on the 5 broken APIs), no batch usage, one `PageIterator`. Resolve the single swing factor (`Microsoft.Graph.ServiceException` under Graph.Core 4.x), fix the latent `DriveItemOperations` dead-catch bug found by the assessment, build green, re-run the Graph-affected tests, and re-smoke the four auth paths + SPE + mail + jobs. ZERO product-behavior change is still the bar — this is a version migration, not a feature change.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Microsoft.Graph .NET SDK v5→v6 migration, Kiota 1→2 abstractions, OBO/Managed-Identity auth, and SPE file operations. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj` references `Microsoft.Graph 6.5.0` (no direct `Microsoft.Kiota.*` pins remain; transitive Kiota = 2.0.0); `NoWarn=NU1903` absent; the `ServiceException`/`ODataError` swing factor resolved; the `DriveItemOperations` dead-catch bug fixed; `dotnet build -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` green; the Graph-affected tests pass; publish hygiene (ADR-029) intact.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner decision 2026-08-11: fold Graph v6 + Kiota 2.0 into THIS project (supersedes the spec's 2026-08-10 "Graph v6 out of scope" resolution). Evidence: `notes/graph6-kiota2-break-assessment.md` — churn buckets: ~1–2 files forced, 6 files contingency-only, 0 moderate, 0 deep. Direct-Kiota surface (`AzureIdentityAuthenticationProvider`, custom `IAccessTokenProvider`, `UntypedObject/String/Boolean` reads in `SpeAdminGraphService`, one `PageIterator` in `PrivilegeGroupResolver`) is all Kiota-2.0-stable; the custom `GraphHttpMessageHandler` is a plain `DelegatingHandler`, not Kiota middleware. Swing factor: does `Microsoft.Graph.ServiceException` survive into Graph.Core 4.x? — evidence says RETAINED (no changelog removal; survived v4→v5). If retained: forced change = 1 csproj + 1 module doc. If removed: delete ~72 `ServiceException` catch blocks across 6 files — but those are ALREADY DEAD on v5 (Kiota throws `ODataError`), so deletion is mechanical. Latent bug to fix in passing: `DriveItemOperations`' `ServiceException` catches are dead today, so its Graph 404/403 fall through as opaque errors — re-anchor them on `ODataError`.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file role="modify">Directory.Build.props</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/graph6-kiota2-break-assessment.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/kiota-cve-finding.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">Full suite green on the net10 / Graph 5.x baseline — the clean bisect point before the Graph major.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Sequence: run AFTER 030 (net10 proven green). Do NOT merge this into the P0 retarget — net10 and the Graph major stay independently verifiable so a bad smoke bisects cleanly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Delete all 7 direct `Microsoft.Kiota.*` pins once Graph 6.5 supplies them transitively at 2.0.0; verify with `dotnet list package --include-transitive | grep -i kiota` that ALL resolved Kiota assemblies are the SAME 2.0.x version (the version-match invariant from the module CLAUDE.md still holds — now enforced transitively). Re-introduce a direct pin ONLY if a transitive conflict forces it, with an inline reason.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">MUST keep `<SelfContained>false</SelfContained>` + `<RuntimeIdentifier>linux-x64</RuntimeIdentifier>`; MUST NOT add `PublishTrimmed`/`PublishAot`/`RuntimeFrameworkVersion`. Report the publish-size delta (Graph 6/Kiota 2 vs 5/1.22) — task 031 re-baselines, but flag if this bump moves it materially (§10 ceiling ≤60 MB).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Auth behavior (OBO + Managed Identity) MUST be unchanged. `AzureIdentityAuthenticationProvider` + the custom `IAccessTokenProvider` are Kiota-2.0-stable — a migration is version-only; do NOT alter token-acquisition flows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Graph access stays behind the `SpeFileStore` facade; do NOT leak `GraphServiceClient` into endpoints during the migration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">ZERO product-behavior change. The two behavior-level verify items (`ODataError.ResponseHeaders` enumeration shape; CAE / backing-store defaults under Kiota 2.0) are SMOKE observations, not source edits — record the observed behavior, do not "fix" it unless it regressed.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Microsoft.Graph v5→v6 + Kiota 1→2 migration on the Spaarke BFF</topic>
