  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj` references `Microsoft.Graph 6.5.0` (or latest 6.x); NO direct `Microsoft.Kiota.*` `PackageReference` remains; `dotnet list package --include-transitive` shows all Kiota assemblies at a single 2.0.x.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` is green; the Graph-affected tests pass; `SelfContained=false` / `linux-x64` / no `PublishTrimmed`/`PublishAot`/`RuntimeFrameworkVersion` are all preserved.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` shows no Kiota HIGH CVE (transitive 2.0.x is > the 1.22.0 floor); `NoWarn=NU1903` is absent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The `DriveItemOperations` dead-catch bug is fixed (404/403 surface via `ODataError`), and the four auth paths + SPE + mail + jobs re-smoke clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no token-acquisition (OBO/MI) flow altered; no `GraphServiceClient` leaked past the `SpeFileStore` facade; no product behavior changed (version migration only).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Owner-approved scope fold-in 2026-08-11 (supersedes spec §Assumptions "Graph v6 out of scope"); evidence `notes/graph6-kiota2-break-assessment.md`. Sequenced after 030; 031 (publish re-baseline) + 032 (CVE audit) run after this so they measure the final Graph-6 graph. This CLOSES the Graph/Kiota deferred major — it comes OFF the design §6.4 deferred list (090 files 5, not 6).

  COMPLETION (2026-08-13): MECHANICAL as the break-assessment predicted — escalation did NOT fire. `Microsoft.Graph` 5.105.0→**6.5.0** → transitive `Graph.Core 4.0.1` + all 7 `Microsoft.Kiota.*` uniformly **2.0.0** (verified `dotnet list --include-transitive`). Deleted all 7 direct Kiota pins; `NoWarn=NU1903` absent; `dotnet list --vulnerable` = no vulnerable packages (CVE-2026-44503 closed transitively; 2.0.0 > 1.22.0 floor). **ServiceException RETAINED** in Graph.Core 4.x → build 0 errors as-is (the ~72 dead ServiceException catches in the other 6 files left harmless per assessment). Fixed the latent **DriveItemOperations** bug: 40 dead `catch (ServiceException) when (ResponseStatusCode==X)` → `catch (ODataError) when (...)` (dead since v4→v5 Kiota rewrite; Graph 404/403/429 fell through to opaque generic catch) — identical predicate structure; Retry-After adapted to ODataError's `IDictionary<string,IEnumerable<string>>` headers via a `GetRetryAfterSeconds` helper (mirrors OfficeExceptionFilter). Behavior-observation: `ODataError.ResponseHeaders` is a plain string-dict (not `ServiceException`'s typed `HttpResponseHeaders.RetryAfter.Delta`) — handled via helper, no product-behavior change. Executed by a sonnet subagent, **independently verified by main session**: build 0 errors + `Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests` **10408 pass/0 fail/101 skip (identical to baseline — zero regression)** + full diff review (40-catch re-anchoring behavior-preserving) + package-graph + CVE + ADR-029 hygiene (`SelfContained=false`/`linux-x64`/no Trimmed/Aot preserved) + ADR-028 auth flows untouched (only exception-catch types changed, no token-acquisition edits). **Publish ~44.06 MB compressed (decrease from ~45.87 MB excl-PDB baseline) → note for task 031 re-baseline.** Watch item for 051 smoke: `Identity.Web.MicrosoftGraph 4.14.2` transitively requests Graph 5.88.0 (resolved up to 6.5.0) — no build/test issue surfaced, but the live OBO-Graph path should be smoke-confirmed at 051. Live 4-auth-path/SPE/mail/jobs smoke deferred to task 051. Graph/Kiota deferred major now CLOSED (090 files 5 deferred majors, not 6). 3 files changed: csproj, DriveItemOperations.cs, module CLAUDE.md. Commit `9e0903bc3`.</notes>

